{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "In crude county shares, Keski-Uusimaa lags the national benchmark only in recorded MDT meetings at 0.0% (95% CI 0.0–0.8; n=0/481) versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The 95% confidence interval for the crude MDT meeting share of 0.0% (95% CI 0.0–0.8; n=0/481) excludes the national 6.0% (893/14873), though HILMO MDT codes WZC15/WZC20 are entered only from direct patient contacts and measure recording practice, not care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In overlapping treatment categories where a patient can have several treatments, Keski-Uusimaa's crude curative treatment share is 33.7% (95% CI 29.6–38.0; n=162/481), whose 95% confidence interval excludes and lies above the national 27.0% (4009/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across the other overlapping treatment categories, crude life-prolonging treatment is 28.9% (95% CI 25.0–33.1; n=139/481) versus 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally and crude symptomatic treatment is 39.5% (95% CI 35.2–43.9; n=190/481) versus 39.5% (5871/14873) nationally, with 95% confidence intervals that include the national values.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "cty:symptomatic:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The crude share with no treatment record within 12 months—which mixes untreated patients and treatment that was not recorded—is 26.4% (95% CI 22.7–30.5; n=127/481), and its 95% confidence interval includes the national 27.5% (4089/14873).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "A journal article shows high diagnosis concordance, but crude county treatment shares lack age and stage adjustment, and public registry data do not measure pathway waiting times.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "lit:hilmo_90",
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Referral",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "The crude county shares have separate limitations: they are not age-adjusted (an age-adjusted value exists only from Kuva 16, for curative treatment, by sex, with digitised national reference lines at ±0.5 percentage points of 26.7% for men and 26.9% for women), and they cannot be stage-adjusted because stage at diagnosis is missing for about 48% of patients.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article reports that HILMO diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, concerning diagnosis concordance only and not treatment, referral or MDT recording, while Finland has no cancer quality registry and lung cancer data reporting, collection and storage are incomplete.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "q:47c7e11303",
          "q:950a2f797b"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public data do not measure symptoms or referrals, do not include outpatient primary care visits in the report's data or mention occupational health, show imaging only indirectly as clinical diagnosis in approximately 20% of patients, and record specialist visits (93.6% within 12 months, up to 3 months before diagnosis) and treatment type within 12 months without wait times.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Preliminary, unpublished national figures show 155 days on average from symptoms to first treatment in Finland versus 107 in Sweden and 67 in Denmark (56 days patient delay, 41 days primary care, 58 days specialist care as the longest stage), while the Health Care Act sets no legal maximum time for a cancer suspicion.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist",
          "law:no_max"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends publishing how completely stage, drug treatment and MDT meetings are recorded, reporting access times using THL 21/2016 guidance, and standardising referrals and diagnostic-phase coordination.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "reg:kys_template",
        "q:950a2f797b"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Given the 0.0% (95% CI 0.0–0.8; n=0/481) crude MDT share and about 48% missing stage nationally, the team recommends publishing per county how completely stage, drug treatment and MDT meetings are recorded—reading gaps as data-quality signals first—while STM roadmap measure 3.2.1 plans a national cancer quality registry (decree updated by 2026–2028; annual reports by 2029–2031 at 90% coverage).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Keski_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695",
          "q:950a2f797b"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because Finland lacks a national system monitoring access to care, the team recommends reporting referral-to-treatment access times using THL guidance Ohjaus 21/2016 definitions for 16 cancers and flagging stalled handovers while STM roadmap measure 3.1.2 plans national cancer-specific pathway descriptions and access times by 2026–2028 and for all significant cancers by 2029–2031.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:4e702a20fe",
          "q:ccda20dce9",
          "q:ed87906241",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:b326e35410"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "As mentor insight notes a weak referral gets a lower urgency rating and regional pathway documents show only KYS provides a referral template and a clear-X-ray persistent-symptoms rule, the team recommends adopting that template and rule while the Filha programme's diagnostics recommendation (referral criteria and time limits) is to be carried out before the 2030 mid-term evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "reg:kys_template",
          "reg:kys_persistent",
          "reg:only_kys_xray",
          "q:29b792498e",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because no reviewed regional pathway document names a diagnostic-phase contact person, the team recommends naming a contact from referral to diagnosis while STM roadmap measure 1.2.3 plans guidance on a named care-coordinator model by 2026–2028, which counties adopt by 2029–2031, with the care phase not specified.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "reg:named_contact",
          "q:fc81032a80",
          "q:abcbb06ae3",
          "q:050ee09ebe"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
